IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35), sections 20 to 29 -- APPEALS TO THE
-- SOCIAL SECURITY TRIBUNAL, AND REFERENCES TO THE TAX COURT OF CANADA ON INCOME.
--
-- Only what these sections decide for the person is encoded: which decisions can be appealed,
-- where a ground of appeal is decided, who is added as a party, where a hearing is held,
-- how the person is told of it, and that no costs or fees arise. How the Tribunal, the
-- Registrar and the judge run the reference (ss 22, 23(3) and (4), 24(1), 25, 27) is inert.

§ `Regulations s 20 -- Appeals`

-- 20(1) to 20(3): which decisions the person may appeal to the Social Security Tribunal.
-- A decision about no benefit, the amount of a benefit, or a penalty is first reconsidered by
-- the Minister under s 18, and only the Minister's decision on that request, under s 18(4),
-- can be appealed (s 20(2)); a decision under s 18(4) or 19(4) can be appealed (s 20(3)).
-- src:221 | 20 (1) For the purposes of section 10.1 of the Act, the body to which a person may appeal is the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
-- src:222 | Paragraphs 10.1(a) and (b) of Act
-- src:223 | (2) A person must follow the procedure set out in section 18 of these Regulations in respect of any requests for reconsideration of decisions referred to in paragraphs 10.1(a) and (b) of the Act. Only a decision of the Minister made under subsection 18(4) of these Regulations in respect of these decisions may be appealed to the Social Security Tribunal.
-- src:224 | Paragraph 10.1(c) of Act
-- src:225 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph 10.1(c) of the Act, a person may appeal to the Social Security Tribunal in respect of any decision of the Minister made under subsection 18(4) or 19(4) of these Regulations.
@ref Regulations s 20(1) to (3) (src:221-225)
GIVEN decision IS A `Decision of the Minister`
GIVETH A `Way to challenge a decision`
`how the person may challenge the decision` decision MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
    WHEN `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` THEN `ask the Minister to reconsider it under section 18`
    WHEN `a decision respecting the amount of a benefit that the person has received or will receive` THEN `ask the Minister to reconsider it under section 18`
    WHEN `a decision imposing a penalty under section 35` THEN `ask the Minister to reconsider it under section 18`
    WHEN `a decision on a request for reconsideration made under subsection 18(4)` THEN `appeal it to the Social Security Tribunal`
    WHEN `a decision on a request for an extension of time made under subsection 19(4)` THEN `appeal it to the Social Security Tribunal`
    WHEN `any other decision` THEN `the text states no route`

§ `Regulations s 21 -- Reference to Court`

DECLARE `Body that decides a ground of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `the Tax Court of Canada, on a reference from the Social Security Tribunal`
    `the Social Security Tribunal`

-- 21(1) and 29: a ground that a decision or determination of the Minister as to income was
-- incorrectly made is referred to the Tax Court of Canada; the other grounds stay with the
-- Tribunal, which proceeds on them after it receives the Court's certified decision.
-- src:227 | 21 (1) If an appeal brought under section 10.1 of the Act includes, as a ground of appeal, a claim or a submission that a decision or determination made by the Minister as to income under the Act was incorrectly made, the Social Security Tribunal must
-- src:228 | (a) notify the appellant and the Minister that the appeal on that ground has been referred to the Court for decision in accordance with subsection 66(2) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act; and
-- src:229 | (b) transmit to the Registrar of the Court a copy of the documents filed in the appeal that are relevant to that ground of appeal.
-- src:261 | 29 If the appellant sets out both a ground of appeal that has been referred to the Court under subsection 66(2) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act and a ground of appeal that has not been referred to the Court under that subsection, the Social Security Tribunal, on receipt of a certified copy of the decision of the Court, must proceed in accordance with the Social Security Tribunal Rules of Procedure.
@ref Regulations s 21(1) (src:227-229); s 29 (src:261)
GIVEN `the ground is a claim or submission that a decision or determination made by the Minister as to income under the Act was incorrectly made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Body that decides a ground of appeal`
`who decides the ground of appeal` `the ground is a claim or submission that a decision or determination made by the Minister as to income under the Act was incorrectly made` MEANS
    IF `the ground is a claim or submission that a decision or determination made by the Minister as to income under the Act was incorrectly made`
    THEN `the Tax Court of Canada, on a reference from the Social Security Tribunal`
    ELSE `the Social Security Tribunal`

-- 29: the Tribunal proceeds on the other grounds once it has the Court's certified decision.
@ref Regulations s 29 (src:261)
GIVEN `the appeal sets out both a ground referred to the Court and a ground not referred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Social Security Tribunal has received a certified copy of the Court's decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Social Security Tribunal must now proceed on the grounds not referred, under its Rules of Procedure` `the appeal sets out both a ground referred to the Court and a ground not referred` `the Social Security Tribunal has received a certified copy of the Court's decision` MEANS
        `the appeal sets out both a ground referred to the Court and a ground not referred`
    AND `the Social Security Tribunal has received a certified copy of the Court's decision`

§ `Regulations s 23 -- Other persons affected`

-- 23(1) and 23(2): where an appeal is about a decision as to income and the Minister is of
-- the opinion that another person may be directly affected by the Court's decision, the
-- Minister must tell the Tribunal, the Tribunal must tell the Registrar, and the Registrar
-- must add that person as a party.
-- src:235 | 23 (1) If an appeal is made in relation to a decision or determination as to income under the Act or these Regulations and the Minister is of the opinion that a person other than the appellant may be directly affected by the decision of the Court, the Minister must so notify the Social Security Tribunal.
-- src:236 | Person added
-- src:237 | (2) The Social Security Tribunal must notify the Registrar of the Court and the Registrar must add that person as a party to the appeal.
@ref Regulations s 23(1) and (2) (src:235-237)
GIVEN `the appeal is in relation to a decision or determination as to income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is of the opinion that a person other than the appellant may be directly affected by the decision of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the other person is added as a party to the appeal` `the appeal is in relation to a decision or determination as to income` `the Minister is of the opinion that a person other than the appellant may be directly affected by the decision of the Court` MEANS
        `the appeal is in relation to a decision or determination as to income`
    AND `the Minister is of the opinion that a person other than the appellant may be directly affected by the decision of the Court`

§ `Regulations s 24 -- Time and place of reference`

-- 24(2): the hearing is in the city, town or village in which, or nearest to which, the
-- appellant is ordinarily resident, unless the appellant consents in writing to another place
-- or to audioconference or videoconference (or both), in whole or in part.
-- src:245 | (2) The hearing of a reference must be held in the city, town or village in which, or nearest to which, the appellant is ordinarily resident unless the appellant consents in writing to the hearing being held, in whole or in part, at some other place or by audioconference or videoconference or a combination of both.
@ref Regulations s 24(2) (src:245)
GIVEN `the appellant consents in writing to the hearing being held, in whole or in part, at some other place or by audioconference or videoconference or a combination of both` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Place of a hearing`
`where the hearing of a reference is held` `the appellant consents in writing to the hearing being held, in whole or in part, at some other place or by audioconference or videoconference or a combination of both` MEANS
    IF `the appellant consents in writing to the hearing being held, in whole or in part, at some other place or by audioconference or videoconference or a combination of both`
    THEN `another place, or by audioconference or videoconference, with the appellant's written consent`
    ELSE `the city, town or village in which, or nearest to which, the appellant is ordinarily resident`

-- 24(3): the Registrar must notify the appellant, by registered mail, of the date, place and
-- time set. The duty arises once they have been set.
-- src:247 | (3) The Registrar of the Court must, by registered mail, notify the appellant, the Social Security Tribunal, the Minister and any person added as a party to the appeal of the date, place and time set for the hearing of the reference.
@ref Regulations s 24(3) (src:247)
GIVEN `the date, place and time of the hearing have been set` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar must notify the appellant by registered mail of the date, place and time` `the date, place and time of the hearing have been set` MEANS
    `the date, place and time of the hearing have been set`

§ `Regulations s 26 -- Written submissions`

-- 26: the judge may require written submissions, in addition to or instead of an oral hearing,
-- only with the appellant's consent.
-- src:253 | 26 The judge appointed to hear the reference may, with the consent of the appellant, require that written submissions be filed by the appellant, the Minister and any person added as a party to the appeal in addition to or in lieu of an oral hearing.
@ref Regulations s 26 (src:253)
GIVEN `the appellant consents to written submissions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the judge may require written submissions` `the appellant consents to written submissions` MEANS
    `the appellant consents to written submissions`

§ `Regulations s 28 -- Costs and fees`

-- 28: no costs may be awarded on the disposition of a reference and no fees may be charged
-- to the appellant by the Court. It depends on nothing.
-- src:259 | 28 No costs may be awarded on the disposition of a reference and no fees may be charged to the appellant by the Court.
@ref Regulations s 28 (src:259)
`costs may be awarded or fees charged to the appellant on a reference` MEANS FALSE
